From 0722074d6b7a55a5391110c4fe7d2c7debf9ab49 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 02:31:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(post): judge the index swing of any work-turning rotary
 about a level line

The index-swing clause (#804, #813) judged only an A about X. A table B
(stated [0,1,0], or unstated and named B) and an A stated level but off
X read "off X" and indexed unjudged. rotary_line now returns the line
itself: Horizontal(unit u) is judged like the microARC A - the tip at
the safe Z (nose_to_axis - tool length) against the farthest turning
vertex from the line through the WCS origin, |(p - o) x u| - with the
same refusal for an unstated nose_to_axis; Vertical (a C) stays safe and
unjudged; a leaning, zero or non-finite vector refuses by name ("not
judged"); no vector and no RS-274 letter still refuses (#813). Two
rotaries turning the work take the sweep from the WCS origin, since each
moves the other's line. A non-finite vertex sweeps without bound
(refused). The pre-#804 load note now names every non-vertical rotary.

Pinned by the new index_swing_horizontal suite over a test-only table-B
machine file; decision in docs/decisions/818-swing-any-horizontal.md.

Fixes #818

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
